    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The leverage of seasonal climate acted as a catalyst, causing the human metric of policy success to spike along the U.S. border. The lever of policy control registered an increase in apprehensions as the numbers told a story of rising pressure in March. Yet, the architects of the deadlock in Washington ensure the political deadlock persists. This creates a stark contrast: the enforcement apparatus successfully maintained border security effect with low crossing numbers, while a legislative stalemate prevents coherent funding for the very system driving those results.",
